# Publishing Sonar Mag articles

Content is **Supabase rows only** — insert/update `articles` and the live Astro site picks it up (short CDN cache). No redeploy for copy.

## Required read

Before writing prose, open and follow [docs/anti-slop-manifesto.md](docs/anti-slop-manifesto.md).

## Homepage (automatic)

| Field | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `status = 'published'` | Eligible for the board |
| `is_highlighted = true` | Eligible for the **large splash hero** (newest highlighted wins) |
| everything else | Fills secondary → opinion → dark card → Latest by `published_at` |
| `popular_rank` | **Do not set manually** — overwritten by Vercel Web Analytics sync (Popular rail / `/popular`) |

You do **not** set `featured_slot` for splash layout anymore.

## Row fields to set

- `slug` (unique), `title`, `excerpt`, `ticker`
  - `excerpt` is the homepage card dek: one continuous ~70–110 word block (CSS columns). Never rely on body paragraphs for card layout.
  - Titles must pass the manifesto clarity test: clever tone without a clear case still fails; study titles must not slogan-oversell.
- `seo_title` — search/browser title only (`<title>`, `og:title`); the on-page `<h1>` stays `title`. Front-load the entity a person would search, say what happened, aim 45–58 chars (`— Sonar Mag` is appended; DB caps at 120). Do not bend `title` toward keywords now that this exists.
- `author_id`, `category_id`
- `hero_image`, `hero_alt`, `thumb_image` — follow manifesto §12a; **must not reuse** another article’s photo (Unsplash `photo-…` id). Same URL for hero+thumb on one row is fine. DB enforces uniqueness via `article_image_key()`. **`hero_alt` is required** whenever `hero_image` is set (concrete scene, not empty / vibe words).
- `read_minutes`, `listen_minutes`, `published_at`, `published_label`
- `paragraphs` jsonb blocks (Markdown **strings** and optional `{ type: "tweet", ... }`)
  - Each string is Markdown (GFM): `**bold**`, `*italic*`, `[links](/path)`, `##`/`###` headings, lists, `>` blockquotes, `` `code` ``, `---`.
  - Prefer one idea per block for the first two strings (they render above the hero figure). After that, blocks may include multi-paragraph Markdown with section headings.
  - Tweet objects stay structured embeds; do not put tweet HTML in Markdown strings.
- `is_highlighted` boolean
- optional: `highlight_word` + `highlight_tone` (`red` \| `tan`) for title mark
- **Do not set `updated_at`** — a trigger maintains it and it feeds `dateModified` / `article:modified_time`. It moves only when an editorial column really changes, so `popular_rank` and `comments_count` syncs leave it alone. Re-saving a row to fake freshness is not allowed.

## Article footer (automatic)

Every article renders a related rail with no authoring work: three cards from the 12 newest published articles (same category first, then recency), plus a "Live scoreboard" card linking `/ai-wars` when the title/ticker/excerpt reads as AI coverage. Do not hand-write "related reading" or generic AI Wars closers.

## Tweet embeds

```json
{
  "type": "tweet",
  "url": "https://x.com/Handle/status/123",
  "authorName": "Display Name",
  "authorHandle": "Handle",
  "text": "Full tweet text…",
  "postedAt": "2026-07-20T10:56:59.000Z"
}
```

Fetch via syndication/fxtwitter when X HTML 403s. Never load Twitter widgets.js.

## Skill

For a two-article batch (one highlighted), use the project skill `write-sonar-articles`.
